<title>JAPAN: Output at big Japan aluminium mills rises in May.</title>
<headline>Output at big Japan aluminium mills rises in May.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Output of fabricated aluminium products at Japan's seven leading mills jumped 8.6 percent in May from the same month last year to 138,826 tonnes, according to data submitted by the companies to the Japan Aluminum Federation and released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The May data was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     May 97	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> Total	    138,826	  +8.6 pct</p>
<p> Flat-rolled    110,977	  +8.3 pct</p>
<p>   Can stock     38,895	  +5.9 pct</p>
<p> Extrusions	27,849	  +9.6 pct</p>
<p>The seven companies are: Kobe Steel Ltd (includes KAAL, a joint venture with Aluminum Co of America ), Sumitomo Light Metal Industries Ltd, Furukawa Electric Co, Mitsubishi Aluminum Co, Nippon Light Metal Co, Sky Aluminium Co and Showa Aluminum Corp.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
